\viewkind4\uc1\pard\qc\cf1\b\fs36 Corpus of Inscriptions of Emperor Ashoka\par
\cf3\b0\i\fs24 Epigraphical Research Division, RTMNU\par
\cf3\i0\fs20 Department of Ancient Indian History, Culture & Archaeology, RTMNU\par\par
\pard\cf2\fs22 Major Rock Edicts, Pillar Inscriptions and Minor Edicts of Devanampriya Priyadarsi.\par\par \par\par Major Rock Edict I (Girnar, Kalsi, Shahbazgarhi, Mansehra):\par\par Here no living being must be killed and sacrificed. Formerly in the kitchen of Beloved-of-the-Gods, King Priyadarsi, many hundreds of thousands of animals were killed every day for curry.\par\par \par\par Major Rock Edict XII:\par\par Beloved-of-the-Gods honors both ascetics and the householders of all religions, and he honors them with gifts and honors of various kinds. Growth in essentials can be done in different ways, but all of them have as their root restraint in speech, that is, not praising one's own religion, or condemning the religion of others without good reason.\par\par \par\par Pillar Edict VII:\par\par Along roads I have had banyan trees planted so that they can give shade to animals and men, and I have had mango groves planted. At intervals of eight kos, I have had wells dug and rest-houses built.\par
}